.TH SPRINTF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sprintf \- format output into an unbounded buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B int sprintf(char *buffer, const char *format);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats output using the Crunch formatter and writes it, including a
terminating NUL, into buffer. The caller must provide enough space; prefer
.BR snprintf (3crunch)
when the capacity is known. The compiler accepts additional numeric and
byte-pointer arguments. Conversion support matches
.BR snprintf (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes written, excluding the terminating NUL, or
\-1 on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snprintf (3crunch),
.BR vsnprintf (3crunch)
